\\ {3}^{x} & =\\frac{1}{{3}^{3}} \\\\ {3}^{x} & ={3}^{-3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since both sides of the equation share the same base $(3)$, we equate the exponents:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{3}^{x} & ={3}^{-3} \\\\ x & =-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=-3.$"] [17592186069358 :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] ["answer-21ce9c20-f571-545e-977f-4d515aced9be" :answer/id #uuid "21ce9c20-f571-545e-977f-4d515aced9be"] ["answer-21ce9c20-f571-545e-977f-4d515aced9be" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-21ce9c20-f571-545e-977f-4d515aced9be" :answer/value "x=-1"] ["answer-4ff56c93-8f4d-5dca-8f7e-6a6a25c4cfda" :answer/id #uuid "4ff56c93-8f4d-5dca-8f7e-6a6a25c4cfda"] ["answer-4ff56c93-8f4d-5dca-8f7e-6a6a25c4cfda" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-4ff56c93-8f4d-5dca-8f7e-6a6a25c4cfda" :answer/value "x=-3"] ["answer-1903a828-2ddb-5f00-80c5-19f5e92b453a" :answer/id #uuid "1903a828-2ddb-5f00-80c5-19f5e92b453a"] ["answer-1903a828-2ddb-5f00-80c5-19f5e92b453a" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-1903a828-2ddb-5f00-80c5-19f5e92b453a" :answer/value "x=1"] ["answer-8994455b-f891-57f8-b13b-45d1a9aa4e96" :answer/id #uuid "8994455b-f891-57f8-b13b-45d1a9aa4e96"] ["answer-8994455b-f891-57f8-b13b-45d1a9aa4e96" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-8994455b-f891-57f8-b13b-45d1a9aa4e96" :answer/value "x=27"] ["answer-15f20d2e-d455-5504-916c-4a9743e14795" :answer/id #uuid "15f20d2e-d455-5504-916c-4a9743e14795"] ["answer-15f20d2e-d455-5504-916c-4a9743e14795" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-15f20d2e-d455-5504-916c-4a9743e14795" :answer/value "x=3"] [17592186067318 :answer-field/correct "answer-4ff56c93-8f4d-5dca-8f7e-6a6a25c4cfda"] [17592186067318 :answer-field/choices "answer-21ce9c20-f571-545e-977f-4d515aced9be"] [17592186067318 :answer-field/choices "answer-4ff56c93-8f4d-5dca-8f7e-6a6a25c4cfda"] [17592186067318 :answer-field/choices "answer-1903a828-2ddb-5f00-80c5-19f5e92b453a"] [17592186067318 :answer-field/choices "answer-8994455b-f891-57f8-b13b-45d1a9aa4e96"] [17592186067318 :answer-field/choices "answer-15f20d2e-d455-5504-916c-4a9743e14795"] ["question-ea72a94a-bdd5-5d3c-b2b4-c2e3488df948" :question/id #uuid "ea72a94a-bdd5-5d3c-b2b4-c2e3488df948"] ["question-ea72a94a-bdd5-5d3c-b2b4-c2e3488df948" :question/math-academy-id "q-208694"] ["question-ea72a94a-bdd5-5d3c-b2b4-c2e3488df948" :question/problem "If $2mn+m+4=7,$ then $m=${{field-1}}."] ["question-ea72a94a-bdd5-5d3c-b2b4-c2e3488df948" :question/worked-solution "We need to isolate all terms with $m$ on one side of the equation. To do this, we subtract $4$ to both sides:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2mn+m+4 & =7 \\\\ 2mn+m+4-4 & =7-4 \\\\ 2mn+m & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we factor out $m$ in the expression on the left-hand side.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2mn+m & =3 \\\\ m(2n+1) & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we divide both sides by $(2n+1)$ to isolate $m:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m(2n+1) & =3 \\\\ \\frac{m(2n+1)}{2n+1} & =\\frac{3}{2n+1} \\\\ \\frac{m\\cancel{(2n+1)}}{\\cancel{2n+1}} & =\\frac{3}{2n+1} \\\\ m & =\\frac{3}{2n+1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Note:** This result assumes that $2n+1\\ne 0.$"] ["question-ea72a94a-bdd5-5d3c-b2b4-c2e3488df948" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] ["answer-field-a2a58eb4-92a4-5719-9dfb-a3aad6a40bc0" :answer-field/id #uuid "a2a58eb4-92a4-5719-9dfb-a3aad6a40bc0"] ["answer-25c699cc-f84c-5b48-8508-432e14803537" :answer/id #uuid "25c699cc-f84c-5b48-8508-432e14803537"] ["answer-25c699cc-f84c-5b48-8508-432e14803537" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-25c699cc-f84c-5b48-8508-432e14803537" :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2n+1}"] ["answer-field-a2a58eb4-92a4-5719-9dfb-a3aad6a40bc0" :answer-field/key "field-1"] ["answer-field-a2a58eb4-92a4-5719-9dfb-a3aad6a40bc0" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank] ["answer-field-a2a58eb4-92a4-5719-9dfb-a3aad6a40bc0" :answer-field/correct "answer-25c699cc-f84c-5b48-8508-432e14803537"] ["answer-field-a2a58eb4-92a4-5719-9dfb-a3aad6a40bc0" :answer-field/choices "answer-25c699cc-f84c-5b48-8508-432e14803537"] ["question-ea72a94a-bdd5-5d3c-b2b4-c2e3488df948" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-a2a58eb4-92a4-5719-9dfb-a3aad6a40bc0"] [17592186179639 :knowledge-point/questions "question-ea72a94a-bdd5-5d3c-b2b4-c2e3488df948"] ["question-af2a1028-5c68-5261-af13-01fa26bc76aa" :question/id #uuid "af2a1028-5c68-5261-af13-01fa26bc76aa"] ["question-af2a1028-5c68-5261-af13-01fa26bc76aa" :question/math-academy-id "q-2765"] ["question-af2a1028-5c68-5261-af13-01fa26bc76aa" :question/problem "Factor the expression $4{r}^{2}+16r+16.$"] ["question-af2a1028-5c68-5261-af13-01fa26bc76aa" :question/worked-solution "Notice that all of the terms have a common factor of $4.$ Therefore, we can simplify the expression by factoring out $4,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{r}^{2}+16r+16 & = \\\\ 4({r}^{2}+4r+4)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's factor the expression inside parentheses using the square of a sum formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{2}+4r+4 & = \\\\ {r}^{2}+4r+{2}^{2} & = \\\\ {r}^{2}+2\\cdot 2r+{2}^{2} & = \\\\ (r+2)^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, our original expression factors as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4({r}^{2}+4r+4) & = \\\\ 4(r+2)^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"] ["question-af2a1028-5c68-5261-af13-01fa26bc76aa" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-field-3f628070-e478-5242-8b4f-a4dea04f863c" :answer-field/id #uuid "3f628070-e478-5242-8b4f-a4dea04f863c"] ["answer-b857f724-d721-59f2-a1ef-b1e614faeab1" :answer/id #uuid "b857f724-d721-59f2-a1ef-b1e614faeab1"] ["answer-b857f724-d721-59f2-a1ef-b1e614faeab1" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-b857f724-d721-59f2-a1ef-b1e614faeab1" :answer/value "(2r+1)^{2}"] ["answer-443effa8-8bc4-55af-875b-6cb18f9954c6" :answer/id #uuid "443effa8-8bc4-55af-875b-6cb18f9954c6"] ["answer-443effa8-8bc4-55af-875b-6cb18f9954c6" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-443effa8-8bc4-55af-875b-6cb18f9954c6" :answer/value "(2r+2)^{2}"] ["answer-81b04f59-9424-5ce4-9b14-2e06ca51b